      reason: The red box sits on the 'Other' row as a write-in text field, not beside
        the Spouse MM/DD/YYYY deceased date fields above it; a filer writes a textual
        description there, matching 'other_special_condition_3_txt' not a date.
      model: claude-sonnet-4-6
      contested: the page check says the name or type does not fit the box
    description: Right-hand continuation of the write-in explanation entered on the
      "Other" line (continuing the preceding write-in boxes); free text, not a date.
    x_petey_review:
      model: claude-opus-5
      changed:
      - type
      - description
      - -semantic_type
      - name
      reason: The 164.6 pt wide box with no max length or comb cannot hold an MM/DD/YYYY
        segment, and the whole-page vision check places it on the "Other" write-in
        row, with the spouse's date of death already captured in the separate MM/DD/YY
        boxes. The name and date typing describe another box, so the field is r
      before:
        type: date
        semantic_type: date
        description: Date of death of the spouse, entered as MM/DD/YYYY beside the
          spouse's name on the 2025 Form 1040 name line.
      old_name: spouse_deceased_dt
      adjudicated: proposed
      judged: 'kept: 2 -> 0'
